# Modularity & Clean Code

Keep views modular, break down components into smaller reusable elements, and follow clean code best practices.

## Core Principles

### 1. Single Responsibility Principle
Each widget should do ONE thing well. If a widget has multiple responsibilities, split it.

### 2. Small, Focused Widgets
Keep reusable widgets under 200 lines where practical. Page/screen files should be gradually split and kept under ~700 lines during migration.

### 3. Composition Over Complexity
Build complex UIs by composing simple widgets, not by creating complex ones.

### 4. Extract and Reuse
If you write similar code twice, extract it into a reusable widget or helper.

## Breaking Down Large Widgets

### BAD - Monolithic widget
```dart
class ChatPage extends StatelessWidget {
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return Scaffold(
      appBar: AppBar(/* 20 lines */),
      body: Column(
        children: [
          // 50 lines of header code
          Container(/* complex header */),
          
          // 100 lines of message list
          ListView.builder(/* complex list */),
          
          // 40 lines of input field
          Container(/* complex input */),
        ],
      ),
    );
  }
}
```

### GOOD - Modular approach
```dart
class ChatPage extends StatelessWidget {
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return Scaffold(
      appBar: _ChatAppBar(),
      body: Column(
        children: [
          _ChatHeader(),
          Expanded(child: _MessageList()),
          _MessageInput(),
        ],
      ),
    );
  }
}

class _ChatHeader extends StatelessWidget { /* focused widget */ }
class _MessageList extends StatelessWidget { /* focused widget */ }
class _MessageInput extends StatelessWidget { /* focused widget */ }
```

## Widget Organization

### Private vs Public Widgets

**Private (_prefix)**: Used only within current file
```dart
class _MessageBubble extends StatelessWidget { }
```

**Public (no prefix)**: Reusable across the app, in `lib/widgets/`
```dart
class PrimaryButton extends StatelessWidget { }
```

### File Structure
```
lib/
  widgets/          # Reusable components
    buttons/
      primary_button.dart
      secondary_button.dart
    inputs/
      glass_text_field.dart
  pages/            # Full screens
    chat_room_page.dart
  models/           # Data models
  providers/        # State management
  constants/        # Theme, colors, etc.
```

## Extract Complex Logic

### BAD - Logic in build method
```dart
Widget build(BuildContext context) {
  return ListView.builder(
    itemBuilder: (context, index) {
      final message = messages[index];
      final isCurrentUser = currentUserId != null && 
                           message.userId == currentUserId;
      final alignment = isCurrentUser ? Alignment.right : Alignment.left;
      final color = isCurrentUser ? Colors.blue : Colors.grey;
      // 30 more lines of logic...
      return Container(/* complex widget */);
    },
  );
}
```

### GOOD - Extract to helper methods
```dart
Widget build(BuildContext context) {
  return ListView.builder(
    itemBuilder: (context, index) => _buildMessageItem(messages[index]),
  );
}

Widget _buildMessageItem(Message message) {
  final isCurrentUser = _isCurrentUser(message);
  return MessageBubble(
    message: message,
    isCurrentUser: isCurrentUser,
  );
}

bool _isCurrentUser(Message message) {
  return currentUserId != null && message.userId == currentUserId;
}
```

## Conditional Rendering

### BAD - Nested ternaries
```dart
child: isLoading ? 
  CircularProgressIndicator() : 
  hasError ? 
    ErrorWidget() : 
    hasData ? 
      DataWidget() : 
      EmptyWidget()
```

### GOOD - Early returns or separate method
```dart
Widget _buildContent() {
  if (isLoading) return CircularProgressIndicator();
  if (hasError) return ErrorState(error: error);
  if (!hasData) return EmptyState();
  return DataWidget(data: data);
}
```

## State Management

### Keep state logic separate from UI
```dart
// BAD - Mixed concerns
class ChatPage extends StatefulWidget {
  State<ChatPage> createState() => _ChatPageState();
}

class _ChatPageState extends State<ChatPage> {
  List<Message> messages = [];
  
  Future<void> fetchMessages() async {
    // 50 lines of API logic mixed with UI
  }
  
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    // 100 lines of UI
  }
}

// GOOD - Separated concerns
class ChatPage extends ConsumerWidget {
  Widget build(BuildContext context, WidgetRef ref) {
    final messages = ref.watch(chatMessagesProvider);
    return _ChatPageContent(messages: messages);
  }
}

// Provider handles all state logic separately
```

## Naming Conventions

### Widget Names
- Descriptive and specific: `MessageInputField` not `InputWidget`
- Prefix with context: `ChatMessageBubble` not `Bubble`

### Methods
- Private helpers: `_buildHeader()`, `_isCurrentUser()`
- Event handlers: `_onSendMessage()`, `_handleSubmit()`

### Variables
- Clear intent: `isCurrentUser` not `isCu`
- Full words: `messageController` not `msgCtrl`

## Constants and Magic Numbers

### BAD - Magic numbers
```dart
Container(
  padding: EdgeInsets.all(16),
  margin: EdgeInsets.only(top: 8, bottom: 12),
  child: Text('Hello', style: TextStyle(fontSize: 14)),
)
```

### GOOD - Named constants
```dart
Container(
  padding: EdgeInsets.all(BleyaTheme.spacingLG),
  margin: EdgeInsets.only(
    top: BleyaTheme.spacingSM,
    bottom: BleyaTheme.spacingMD,
  ),
  child: Text('Hello', style: BleyaTheme.bodySmall),
)
```

## Comments

### When to Comment
- **Complex business logic**: Why this approach was chosen
- **Workarounds**: Why this hack exists
- **Non-obvious code**: What might confuse future developers

### When NOT to Comment
- **Obvious code**: Don't comment what the code already says
- **Bad code**: Refactor instead of explaining

```dart
// BAD - Obvious comment
// Create a list of messages
List<Message> messages = [];

// GOOD - Explains non-obvious business logic
// Messages are cached for 5 minutes to reduce API calls
// while ensuring users see reasonably fresh data
final cachedMessages = _getCachedMessages(maxAge: Duration(minutes: 5));
```

## Checklist for Every Widget/Page

- [ ] Reusable widget is under 200 lines (extract if larger)
- [ ] Page/screen file is under ~700 lines (split sections into widgets over time)
- [ ] One clear responsibility
- [ ] Complex sections extracted to smaller widgets
- [ ] Logic extracted from build method
- [ ] No magic numbers (use theme constants)
- [ ] Descriptive names for widgets and variables
- [ ] Reusable components used from `lib/widgets/`
- [ ] State management separated from UI

